## 7. Measured starter-topic expansion

Current starter topics are Free Discussion, Gaming Hangout, Movie Chat, and Metalheads. Each topic has one Persian and one English instance, for eight current starter-room instances across two languages.

☐ Collect privacy-light aggregate metrics for:
- onboarding Interest-chip selections by normalized predefined chip key;
- starter-room previews, joins, active members, messages, and reports;
- rooms that repeatedly approach capacity;
- rooms that remain empty or inactive.

☐ After the first rollout has enough real usage, consider this initial eight-topic catalog:
- Free Discussion;
- Movies;
- Gaming;
- Music;
- Books;
- Technology;
- Sports;
- Everyday Life.

If all eight topics are enabled in both Persian and English, there will be 16 starter-room instances—not eight languages.

☐ Add a topic only when onboarding selections and discussion activity show clear demand. Do not enable every candidate automatically.

☐ For each added topic:
- define a stable seed key and bilingual title/description;
- use a broad predefined onboarding Interest chip for a simple, understandable join rule;
- seed separate Persian and English rooms;
- preserve idempotent seeding and stable ordering;
- include the room in matching-invitation tests and discovery ranking tests;
- verify the rule explains exactly how a locked user can become eligible.

☐ Keep one open Free Discussion fallback per language regardless of topic expansion.

☐ Do not delete inactive rooms or their user data automatically. Hide/close an inactive Muze room only through a separately reviewed migration that accounts for current members and notifications.

☐ Add numbered overflow rooms only when a starter topic repeatedly approaches its effective capacity. Route new onboarding invitations to an open, non-full instance in the correct language, preferring a healthy active room without concentrating every user into one room.

☐ Before adding overflow logic, define:
- the occupancy threshold and observation window;
- whether routing prefers least-full or most-active-with-capacity;
- how room numbering/titles appear to users;
- how discovery avoids showing many near-identical rooms;
- how moderators monitor reports and activity across instances;
- whether an overflow room may be closed after becoming inactive, without moving users or copying messages automatically.

☐ Validate any topic/overflow expansion with unit tests, discussion integration tests, translation validation, bilingual smoke tests, and updated operational dashboard counts.

## Definition of done

- Every normal onboarding completion either has one valid invitation or makes no invitation promise.
- Muze starter rooms support 100 members without changing user-created rooms.
- Discussions, Favorites, and People teach their purpose once and remain low-noise afterward.
- Existing contextual join errors, profile growth hints, saved-profile empty states, Stars, Guide, invitations, and navigation behavior remain intact.
- Additional starter topics and overflow instances are introduced only from measured demand, with separate Persian and English rooms and no destructive automatic retirement.
- Translation, unit, integration, diff, and bilingual manual checks pass.
